// Example scene (WP12.1): content/briefings/EXAMPLE-bridge.fountain converted with
//     cargo run -p sf_cutscene --bin fountain2scene -- \
//         content/briefings/EXAMPLE-bridge.fountain assets/scenes/example_bridge.ron
// and then checked by hand. The generated skeleton was correct as it came out; the
// hand edits only add what a Fountain note cannot say, each marked `hand edit`:
//   - arrows and pins on the map overlay,
//   - Oda steps towards the major while she speaks (a Move with easing),
//   - the major points when he gives the order (a pose change),
//   - a slow push-in during that order (CameraZoom) and a shake on the explosion.
// Everything else is generator output. Figures are geometric placeholders
// (docs/cutscene-format.md); there are no files to be missing, the sound slots are
// silent (`sound: None`, the writer's wish is in `note`).
// `// line N` after an event is the line in the Fountain file it came from.
#![enable(implicit_some)]
